<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — Recorded-Path picker dialog (Avalonia view).

    1:1 visual + behavioural PARITY reimplementation of the deleted WinForms
    `Forms/Pickers/FormRecordPicker` (FormRecordPicker.cs + FormRecordPicker.Designer.cs).
    It lists the *.rec recorded driving paths found in the current field directory and lets the
    operator load one ("Use Selected"), delete one ("Delete Record"), turn the recorded path off
    ("Path Off"), or cancel. Per AAP §0.3.3 this is a faithful parity reimplementation of the
    current Windows Forms look — never a redesign: no new colours, no relayout, no UX changes.

    WIRING CONTRACT — this view is a CODE-BEHIND dialog, NOT MVVM (exactly like the sibling
    FormYesView / FormInputDialogView):
      * There is intentionally NO x:DataType, NO DataContext and NO {Binding} on the controls
        themselves. The partner code-behind (FormRecordPickerView.axaml.cs) owns ALL behaviour and
        addresses every control imperatively BY x:Name — it assigns lvLines.ItemsSource (the list
        of .rec record names), sets the translated caption text (chName / labelPathOff /
        labelDeleteRecord / labelCancel / btnOpenText via gStr), and subscribes to the four button
        Click events. Consequently NO Click handlers are declared in this markup (the handler
        method names live solely in the code-behind); the named controls below MUST keep these
        exact x:Names so the code-behind compiles and binds against them:
        lvLines, chName, btnTurnOffRecPath, labelPathOff, btnDeleteField, labelDeleteRecord,
        btnDeleteAB, labelCancel, buttonOpenExistingLv, btnOpenText.
      * Behaviour preserved from FormRecordPicker.cs: buttonOpenExistingLv (WinForms
        DialogResult.Yes) loads the selected .rec and closes returning true; btnDeleteAB (WinForms
        DialogResult.Cancel) closes; btnTurnOffRecPath stops/clears the recorded path then closes;
        btnDeleteField deletes the selected .rec and stays open (re-loads the list).

    WINDOW SHELL — mirrors FormRecordPicker.Designer.cs exactly:
      ClientSize 972 x 578        -> Width / Height (SystemDecorations="None" => client == window).
      ControlBox = false          -> covered by the borderless (SystemDecorations="None") shell.
      (Fixed, not resizable)      -> CanResize="False".
      ShowInTaskbar = false       -> ShowInTaskbar="False".
      StartPosition CenterParent  -> WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner" (shown modally over FormGPS).
      Font Tahoma 14.25pt         -> FontFamily="Tahoma" FontSize="19" (14.25pt x 96/72 = 19 DIP).
      NO BackColor was set in the Designer -> NO Background here: the window keeps the FluentTheme
      default chrome (the WinForms "default control" look), adapting to the app day/night variant.
      The source did NOT set TopMost, so this dialog is intentionally NOT Topmost.

    Button glyphs are served from the GPS assembly via avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/<name>.png
    (SwitchOff / Trash / Cancel64 / FileOpen — all 64 x 64 on disk), matching the file casing and
    the avares:// convention already used by the sibling GPS views (FormYesView / SelectFieldMenuView).
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.Pickers.FormRecordPickerView"
        Title="FormRecordPicker"
        Width="972"
        Height="578"
        SystemDecorations="None"
        CanResize="False"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        FontFamily="Tahoma"
        FontSize="19">

    <!--
        Shared flat/transparent image-button style. The WinForms buttons were FlatStyle.Flat with
        FlatAppearance.BorderSize = 0 and an image-only (or image+text) face. This class reproduces
        that: a transparent, border-less face that stays transparent through hover/pressed (the
        Fluent Button template otherwise paints a hover/pressed fill). The pointerover/pressed
        setters target the template content presenter — the same technique used by FormYesView and
        Keypad/NumKeypad.axaml.
    -->
    <Window.Styles>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
    </Window.Styles>

    <!--
        Root Canvas reproducing the WinForms absolute layout verbatim (the form is fixed-size, so
        absolute coordinates are exact and the WinForms Anchors are moot). Every child is placed
        with Canvas.Left / Canvas.Top equal to its WinForms Designer Location, at its Designer Size.
    -->
    <Canvas>

        <!--
            lvLines — recorded-path list. WinForms ListView (View=Details) at Location (5,12),
            Size 967 x 459, BackColor InactiveCaption (~#FFBFCDDB, matching the sibling pickers),
            single "Record Name" column (Width 680), FullRowSelect, GridLines, MultiSelect=false,
            HideSelection=false, Sorting=Ascending, Font Tahoma 21.75pt.

            Avalonia has no Details-ListView, so the region is a Border at the exact rectangle
            holding a 2-row Grid: a non-scrolling column-header row (chName) above the scrolling
            ListBox. The header sits inside the 459px region — exactly as the WinForms Details
            header is part of the 459px control — for column-header parity.
        -->
        <Border Canvas.Left="5"
                Canvas.Top="12"
                Width="967"
                Height="459"
                Background="#FFBFCDDB"
                BorderBrush="#FF808080"
                BorderThickness="1">
            <Grid RowDefinitions="Auto,*">

                <!-- chName — the single "Record Name" column header (Width 680 like the WinForms
                     ColumnHeader). Non-scrolling (outside the ListBox), with a 1px divider beneath
                     it standing in for the Details header separator. Text is the Designer default
                     and is (re)assigned by the code-behind. -->
                <Border Grid.Row="0"
                        BorderBrush="#FFA0A0A0"
                        BorderThickness="0,0,0,1">
                    <TextBlock x:Name="chName"
                               Text="Record Name"
                               Width="680"
                               HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                               FontFamily="Tahoma"
                               FontSize="16"
                               Padding="8,4" />
                </Border>

                <!-- lvLines — the record rows. ItemsSource (a list of record-name strings) is
                     assigned by the code-behind; SelectionMode="Single" mirrors MultiSelect=false.
                     HorizontalContentAlignment=Stretch on the item container reproduces
                     FullRowSelect (the selection highlight spans the whole row). Font 29 DIP =
                     21.75pt. Background matches the region so the list reads as one InactiveCaption
                     panel. -->
                <ListBox x:Name="lvLines"
                         AutomationProperties.Name="Recorded path list"
                         Grid.Row="1"
                         Background="#FFBFCDDB"
                         BorderThickness="0"
                         FontFamily="Tahoma"
                         FontSize="29"
                         SelectionMode="Single">
                    <ListBox.Styles>
                        <Style Selector="ListBoxItem">
                            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
                            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="8,2" />
                        </Style>
                    </ListBox.Styles>
                    <ListBox.ItemTemplate>
                        <DataTemplate>
                            <!-- Each item is a plain record-name string; {Binding} (no path) binds
                                 to the string itself (reflection binding — no x:DataType needed). -->
                            <TextBlock Text="{Binding}"
                                       FontFamily="Tahoma"
                                       FontSize="29"
                                       VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                        </DataTemplate>
                    </ListBox.ItemTemplate>
                </ListBox>

            </Grid>
        </Border>

        <!--
            btnDeleteField — deletes the selected .rec then stays open (re-loads the list). WinForms
            Location (47,503), Size 71 x 63, image-only (Resources.Trash, 64 x 64). Caption label
            labelDeleteRecord sits just above it at (41,489), Tahoma 9.75pt (= 13 DIP). The label
            Text is the Designer default and is (re)assigned by the code-behind (gStr.gsDelete).
        -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="labelDeleteRecord"
                   Canvas.Left="41"
                   Canvas.Top="489"
                   Text="Delete Record"
                   FontFamily="Tahoma"
                   FontSize="13" />
        <Button x:Name="btnDeleteField"
                Classes="flatImage"
                Canvas.Left="47"
                Canvas.Top="503"
                Width="71"
                Height="63"
                AutomationProperties.Name="Delete Record">
            <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/Trash.png"
                   Width="63"
                   Height="63"
                   Stretch="Uniform" />
        </Button>

        <!--
            btnTurnOffRecPath — stops + clears the recorded path then closes. WinForms Location
            (223,502), Size 71 x 63, image-only (Resources.SwitchOff). Caption label labelPathOff
            at (230,489); Text reassigned by the code-behind (gStr.gsTurnOffRecordedPath).
        -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="labelPathOff"
                   Canvas.Left="230"
                   Canvas.Top="489"
                   Text="Path Off"
                   FontFamily="Tahoma"
                   FontSize="13" />
        <Button x:Name="btnTurnOffRecPath"
                Classes="flatImage"
                Canvas.Left="223"
                Canvas.Top="502"
                Width="71"
                Height="63"
                AutomationProperties.Name="Turn Off Recorded Path">
            <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/SwitchOff.png"
                   Width="63"
                   Height="63"
                   Stretch="Uniform" />
        </Button>

        <!--
            btnDeleteAB — the Cancel button (WinForms DialogResult.Cancel). Location (565,503),
            Size 71 x 63, image-only (Resources.Cancel64). Caption label labelCancel at (576,489);
            Text reassigned by the code-behind (gStr.gsCancel).
        -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="labelCancel"
                   Canvas.Left="576"
                   Canvas.Top="489"
                   Text="Cancel"
                   FontFamily="Tahoma"
                   FontSize="13" />
        <Button x:Name="btnDeleteAB"
                Classes="flatImage"
                Canvas.Left="565"
                Canvas.Top="503"
                Width="71"
                Height="63"
                AutomationProperties.Name="Cancel">
            <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/Cancel64.png"
                   Width="63"
                   Height="63"
                   Stretch="Uniform" />
        </Button>

        <!--
            buttonOpenExistingLv — "Use Selected" (WinForms DialogResult.Yes): loads the selected
            .rec and closes returning true. Location (702,502), Size 261 x 63, BackColor Transparent,
            Tahoma 18pt (= 24 DIP), image (Resources.FileOpen) ImageAlign MiddleLeft + Text
            MiddleRight + TextImageRelation ImageBeforeText -> a horizontal StackPanel of the FileOpen
            glyph followed by the btnOpenText caption. btnOpenText.Text is reassigned by the
            code-behind (gStr.gsUseSelected).
        -->
        <Button x:Name="buttonOpenExistingLv"
                Classes="flatImage"
                Canvas.Left="702"
                Canvas.Top="502"
                Width="261"
                Height="63"
                FontFamily="Tahoma"
                FontSize="24"
                AutomationProperties.Name="Use Selected">
            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/FileOpen.png"
                       Width="48"
                       Height="48"
                       Stretch="Uniform"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                <TextBlock x:Name="btnOpenText"
                           Text="Use Selected"
                           FontFamily="Tahoma"
                           FontSize="24"
                           VerticalAlignment="Center"
                           Margin="8,0,0,0" />
            </StackPanel>
        </Button>

    </Canvas>
</Window>
